From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:39:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Release 0.3.0: Add the user manual, examples and
 performance evidence

Bump the version to 0.3.0 and give the crate and sdist an explicit file
list. Add docs/user-manual.md, whose Python blocks
validation/release_checks.py now executes; examples/python with four
application and four optimization examples (SciPy and fcmaes) and their
saved outputs; examples/matrix_scan.rs and examples/breakdown.rs; and
validation/run_examples.py and validation/python_call_costs.py. Update
the architecture guide with the 0.3.0 design and measured performance,
and the README, tutorial and model card. Record the cumulative native
table, the time breakdown, Python per-call costs and the installed
Python optimization runs under evidence/performance-0.3.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
